<Layout title="Cancellations & refunds"><PageHero eyebrow="CANCELLATIONS & REFUNDS" title="Know the terms before paying." text="Your written service agreement should clearly explain what happens if your plans change."/><article class="container prose"><h2>Before a payment is requested</h2><p>Ask Verto for the cancellation and refund terms that apply to your service. They should explain the work covered by the fee, when work begins, how work already completed is treated and how to request cancellation. This website does not promise an automatic full refund or state that every payment is non-refundable.</p><h2>Requesting a cancellation or refund</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:travel@vertoimmigrationinc.com">travel@vertoimmigrationinc.com</a> with your name, registration reference, payment date and a brief explanation. Do not include your card number or sensitive identity documents. Verto will review the request against your agreement, work completed and applicable law.</p><h2>Government and third-party payments</h2><p>Government fees, medical examinations, translations and other third-party charges may have separate refund rules. Confirm who is charging each fee and where any refund request must be directed.</p><h2>An immigration refusal</h2><p>A refusal does not by itself determine whether a service fee is refundable. Your service agreement and applicable law govern that question. No service fee purchases or guarantees an approval.</p><div class="notice">Do not proceed with payment if the service scope, merchant identity or refund terms are unclear. <a href="/contact/">Contact Verto first</a>.</div></article></Layout>
